Alembic migrations for the ecomsbd backend.

Rules (master spec section 109):

  1. Every schema change ships as a migration; no ad-hoc DDL, ever.
  2. Deploys are backward compatible where possible: expand -> migrate -> contract.
  3. Data backfills are separate from the blocking DDL transaction.
  4. Never drop a column the previous running server version still reads.
  5. Every migration is tested against a production-like copy before release.

Commands (from backend/):

  alembic upgrade head          apply
  alembic downgrade -1          roll back one revision
  alembic revision --autogenerate -m "..."   draft from model changes
  alembic history --verbose     inspect

Autogenerate drafts a migration; it does not review one. Always read the
generated file, especially for anything touching a money column.
